  s0: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set)
  s1: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set, the hub's file says otherwise, 1 file edit so far)
  s2: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far)
  s3: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input waits at the gateway
  s4: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input is kept for the designated node
  s5: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input is kept for the designated node, the waiting input was cleared
  s6: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input is handed to the designated node, the waiting input was cleared
  s7: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), the designated node's worker claimed an input that has not begun, the waiting input was cleared
  s8: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), turn runs on the designated node [a cleared input ran]
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: an operator edits one node's config file
  s1 --> s2: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s2 --> s3: you send a message
  s3 --> s4: the gateway puts the input into shared custody
  s4 --> s5: you run /clear at the gateway
  s5 --> s6: the input is handed to the node that owns the channel
  s6 --> s6: a node reads the owner row again
  s6 --> s7: the home's worker claims the input
  s7 --> s8: the input begins in a session of the current generation
